\details{
\subsection{Projected Change in Catchability}{

In projection years, simulated index values are
\code{Efficiency * NomIndex_t^Beta * Error_t * (1 + qInc / 100)^(t - t_H)},
where \code{t - t_H} is the time in years since the last historical time step
(a fraction of a year for each season of a seasonal model). The multiplier
is 1 in the historical period, so \code{qInc} has no effect on historical data,
conditioning on real data, or \code{Ref}. Index values supplied for projection
years in \code{OM@Data} are used as-is.
}

\subsection{Observation Error Generation}{

The \code{Error} array (\verb{nSim x nYear}) is obtained in one of three ways, in
order of precedence:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{User-supplied \code{Error}}: stored directly; \code{CV} is not used.
\item \strong{Stochastic from \code{CV}}: if \code{Error} is \code{NULL} and \code{CV} is specified,
Internally the model generates a lognormal array where each cell is
\code{rlnorm(1, mconv(1, CV[sim]), sdconv(1, CV[sim]))}. \code{CV} is first
expanded to length \code{nSim} internally — a length-2 input
triggers a stochastic draw of a unique CV per simulation.
\item \strong{Conditioned from real data}: \code{\link[=Simulate]{Simulate()}} sets the historical years
of \code{Error} from the residuals between the observed and simulated index,
and generates projection years from \code{CV} and \code{AC} (see "Conditioning on
Real Data").
}

\code{Ref} is expanded internally: a scalar is treated as the CV of
a lognormal from which one reference value multiplier per simulation is
drawn; a length-\code{nSim} input is used directly.
}

\subsection{Conditioning on Real Data}{

When real index data are provided (via \code{OM@Data}), \code{\link[=Simulate]{Simulate()}}
conditions the observation model and the following slots are estimated:
\itemize{
\item \code{Efficiency} (\code{q}) is always fit per simulation by log-linear regression
of \code{log(Observed)} on \code{log(NomIndex)}, under
\code{Observed_t = Efficiency * NomIndex_t^Beta * Error_t}, and multiplied by
the mean of the exponentiated log-residuals (smearing correction), so the
historical \code{Error} has mean 1, as the projection \code{Error} does. \code{Beta} is jointly estimated
the same way, but only when \code{SimControl(EstimateBeta = TRUE)} and the
user has not already supplied a value for that index; otherwise \code{Beta}
is held fixed (at the user's value, or \code{1}). When estimated, each
simulation gets an explicit fit \code{Status} (\code{"estimated"},
\code{"fixed_low_variance"}, \code{"fixed_not_significant"},
\code{"fixed_bounds"}, ...) plus \code{SE_Beta}, a confidence interval, \code{R2}, and
\code{PValue}, stored in \code{Misc$BetaFit} (see \code{\link[=EstimateBeta]{EstimateBeta()}}) and
summarized by \code{\link[=IndexFitTable]{IndexFitTable()}}.
\item \code{Stats}: a data frame computed by \code{\link[=CalcResidualStats]{CalcResidualStats()}} with columns
\code{Sim}, \code{AC} (weighted lag-1 autocorrelation of log-residuals), \code{SD}
(standard deviation of log-residuals), and \code{NA_Season} (a list-column
indicating which seasons, if any, have no observations in any year).
\item \code{AC} and \code{CV}: values supplied by the user before conditioning are kept
and used for projection years. Otherwise they are set from \code{Stats$AC}
and \code{Stats$SD} (the latter converted from log-scale SD to CV via the
inverse of \code{\link[=sdconv]{sdconv()}}).
\item \code{Error}: the historical years are the residuals, with mean 1, so historical data
match the observed index. The projection years are taken from a
user-supplied \code{Error}, or else generated by \code{\link[=GenResiduals]{GenResiduals()}} from \code{CV}
and \code{AC}, starting from the last historical residual.
}

\code{Stats} always holds the estimated residual statistics. Values are
recorded as user-supplied in \code{Misc$UserSupplied} when the object is
populated.
}

\subsection{Selectivity Notes}{

Index selectivity is set only on the \link[=indicesobs-class]{indicesobs} object, and is used
both when conditioning on real index data and when generating simulated
index data. CPUE indices named after a fleet use that fleet's selectivity
when \code{Selectivity} is \code{NULL}. Survey indices must set \code{Selectivity} with one
of the forms described under the \code{Selectivity} parameter.
}

